course: dictionary
lesson: 4614
title: Hideous: ugly and horrible
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture in your head, and hideous is one of them. It means extremely ugly, or horrible to look at. Writers use it for monsters, trolls and nasty faces, so the reader can picture something frightening.
explain: Hideous can also mean very unpleasant or shocking, as in a hideous crime or a hideous noise. Look at the words around it to find the right meaning: a hideous monster is about how it looks, but a hideous noise is about how it sounds.
explain: Gran asks Ruby, «D'you love it, pet?» about a bright orange jumper with a purple llama. «Ruby thinks it's hideous», but she is too kind to say so. The context tells you that hideous here means ugly, and that Ruby is being polite.
explain: Be kind with this word. People often joke that a jumper or wallpaper is hideous, but calling a person hideous is very hurtful. Keep it for monsters, nasty things and jumpers, never for people.
fact: Hideous is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a hideous monster, a hideous noise.
fact: Its forms are hideous, more hideous and most hideous.
fact: «Hideous» means extremely ugly or horrible to look at.
fact: «Hideous» also means very unpleasant or shocking, like a hideous crime.
fact: Calling a person hideous is very hurtful, so use it for monsters and things, not people.
exercise: Gran asks, «D'you love it, pet?» Ruby thinks the jumper is hideous. What does hideous mean? | *Extremely ugly | Very soft and warm | Very small | Brand new
exercise: Which phrase uses hideous to mean very unpleasant or shocking? | *a hideous crime | a hideous monster | a bright orange jumper | a soft blanket
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means ugly and horrible: «The hideous troll roared at the children.» | *hideous | troll | children | roared
test: Why should you never call a person hideous? | It means they are very tall | *It is very hurtful | It is too long a word | It is only used for jumpers
test: Which form is the strongest, the one for the most extreme case? | more hideous | hideousest | *most hideous | hideously
exam: Ruby says, «The monster's hideous roar made everyone shiver.» Which meaning fits best? | Soft and warm | *Very unpleasant and frightening, so the roar is horrible to hear | Very quiet, like a whisper | Bright and colourful
